			<attribute key="id" type="int">28</attribute>
			<attribute key="label" type="String">To construct the message "Hello Kiran !!!", two methods are provided below.


*** Method 1 ***
let name = input();
let greeting = "Hello " + name + " !!!";


*** Method 2 ***
let name = input();
let partMsg = "Hello " + name;
let greeting = partMsg + " !!!";

Rahul says Method 1 is wrong becuase we should use only one + operator i n one statement.

Sameer says Method 2 is wrong because the greeting will be printed as 2 separate lines of output.

Who is correct?
</attribute>
